"Chromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of Sn (https://alco.centre-mersenne.org/item/10.5802/alco.134.pdf)\nciteturn4search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.7 years ago; Chromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of Sₙ ... We also introduce the pointed chromatic symmetric function X_{G,v} associated to a rooted graph (G,v). ... Stanley and Stembridge conjectured a stronger claim, that such \\(X_G\\) are positive in the basis of elementary symmetric functions, and this conjecture remains open [12].\nAlgebraic Combinatorics  \nVolume 5, issue 1 (2022), p. 1–20  \nhttps://doi.org/10.5802/alco.134\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nSmall colored geometric logo at upper right, a hexagonal cube-like mosaic in blue, pink, beige, and black outline.\n</visual_element>\n\nChromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of Sₙ\n\nBrendan Pawlowski\n\n**Abstract** We prove some Schur positivity results for the chromatic symmetric function X_G of a (hyper)graph G, using connections to the group algebra of the symmetric group. The first such connection works for (hyper)forests F: we describe the Schur coefficients of X_F in terms of eigenvalues of a product of Hermitian idempotents in the group algebra, one factor for each edge (a more general formula of similar shape holds for all chordal graphs). Our main application of this technique is to prove a conjecture of Taylor on the Schur positivity of certain X_F, which implies Schur positivity of the formal group laws associated to various combinatorial generating functions. We also introduce the pointed chromatic symmetric function X_{G,v} associated to a rooted graph (G,v). We prove that if X_{G,v} and X_{H,w} are positive in the generalized Schur basis of Strahov, then the chromatic symmetric function of the wedge sum of (G,v) and (H,w) is Schur positive.\n\n## 1. INTRODUCTION\n\nLet G be a finite simple graph with vertices V and edges E. A coloring of G is a function κ : V → N, and κ is proper if (v,w) ∈ E implies κ(v) ≠ κ(w).\n\n**Definition 1.1** ([9]). The chromatic symmetric function of G is the formal power series\n\n\\[\nX_G = \\sum_{\\kappa} x_{\\kappa},\n\\]\n\nwhere κ runs over proper colorings of G and \\(x_{\\kappa} = \\prod_{v \\in V} x_{\\kappa(v)}\\).\n\nThe specialization \\(X_G(1,\\ldots,1,0,0,\\ldots)\\) recovers the more classical chromatic polynomial \\(\\chi_G(k)\\). Being a symmetric function, \\(X_G\\) is a linear combination of Schur functions, and the question we are concerned with here is when these coefficients are nonnegative, i.e. when \\(X_G\\) is Schur positive. We will often say “G is Schur positive” to mean that \\(X_G\\) is Schur positive.\n\nThe best-known result of this type is due to Gasharov [3]: if P is a (3 + 1)-free poset (does not contain the disjoint union of a 3-chain and a 1-chain as a subposet), and G is its incomparability graph (the graph on P with an edge (x,y) whenever x and y are incomparable in P), then \\(X_G\\) is Schur positive. Stanley and Stembridge conjectured a stronger claim, that such \\(X_G\\) are positive in the basis of elementary symmetric functions, and this conjecture remains open [12].\n\nManuscript received 30th July 2018, revised 1st May 2020, accepted 13th June 2020.  \nKeywords. Chromatic symmetric function, pointed chromatic symmetric function, Schur positivity.\n\nISSN: 2589-5486                                                                             http://algebraic-combinatorics.org/--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of $S_n$ (https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05470)\nciteturn4academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.7 years ago; Title: Chromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of $S_n$ ... Our main application of this technique is to prove a conjecture of Taylor on the Schur positivity of certain $X_F$, which implies Schur positivity of the formal group laws associated to various combinatorial generating functions. We also introduce the pointed chromatic symmetric function $X_{G,v}$ associated to a rooted graph $(G,v)$.\nTitle: Chromatic symmetric functions via the group algebra of $S_n$\nAuthors: Brendan Pawlowski\nDate: Thu Feb 15 10:40:37 2018\n\nWe prove some Schur positivity results for the chromatic symmetric function $X_G$ of a (hyper)graph $G$, using connections to the group algebra of the symmetric group. The first such connection works for (hyper)forests $F$: we describe the Schur coefficients of $X_F$ in terms of eigenvalues of a product of Hermitian idempotents in the group algebra, one factor for each edge (a more general formula of similar shape holds for all chordal graphs). Our main application of this technique is to prove a conjecture of Taylor on the Schur positivity of certain $X_F$, which implies Schur positivity of the formal group laws associated to various combinatorial generating functions. We also introduce the pointed chromatic symmetric function $X_{G,v}$ associated to a rooted graph $(G,v)$. We prove that if $X_{G,v}$ and $X_{H,w}$ are positive in the generalized Schur basis of Strahov, then the chromatic symmetric function of the wedge sum of $(G,v)$ and $(H,w)$ is Schur positive.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALGEBRAIC\nCOMBINATORICS\nBrendan Pawlowski\nChromati (https://www.numdam.org/item/ALCO_2022__5_1_1_0.pdf)\nciteturn4search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; Chromatic symmetric functions via the ... a (hyper)graph G, using connections to the group algebra of the symmetric group. ... We also introduce the pointed chromatic symmetric function XG,v associated to a ... symmetric functions, and this conjecture remains open [12].\nAlgebraic Combinatorics\nVolume 5, issue 1 (2022), p. 1–20\nhttps://doi.org/10.5802/alco.134\nChromatic symmetric functions via the\ngroup algebra of Sn\nBrendan Pawlowski\nAbstract We prove some Schur positivity results for the ch